From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Mon, 05 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman_port: reserve the vendor 96 B RX internal margin + parse start offset

Push-only VLAN offload (untagged ingress -> tagged egress) is the one
inline FE-VM case that grows the frame in front of its start. With
mainline's FMBM_RIM = 0 / FMBM_RPSO = 0 the ingress port wedged RX-deaf
within ~10 hits in every record form tried, vendor-exact opcodes and
stats pointers included (.185, 2026-10-05). The vendor SDK programs
RIM 0x60000000 / RPSO 0x60 on every RX port (read live on .106).

Writing those two registers live on .185 made push-only offload deliver
VID 10 at line rate with the port healthy. The full rig matrix (unidir
and bidir, v4/v6, vlan->vlan, vlan->port, port->port) ran with no
regression and both ports stayed healthy.

Program the same values in init_bmi_rx(): internal margin
max(int_buf_start_margin, 96) and parse start offset 96.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
index 17ea7b1..601767e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
@@ -113,6 +113,7 @@
 
 #define BMI_INT_BUF_MARG_SHIFT			28
 #define BMI_INT_BUF_MARG_MASK			0x0000000f
+#define FMAN_PORT_RX_HM_MARGIN			96	/* vendor RIM/RPSO, bytes */
 #define BMI_EXT_BUF_MARG_START_SHIFT		FMAN_SP_EXT_BUF_MARG_START_SHIFT
 #define BMI_EXT_BUF_MARG_START_MASK		0x000001ff
 #define BMI_EXT_BUF_MARG_END_MASK		0x000001ff
@@ -572,10 +573,21 @@ static int init_bmi_rx(struct fman_port *port)
 		BMI_IC_SIZE_MASK;
 	iowrite32be(tmp, &regs->fmbm_ricp);
 
-	/* Internal buffer offset */
-	tmp = ((cfg->int_buf_start_margin / PORT_IC_OFFSET_UNITS) &
+	/* Internal buffer offset. The FE-VM inline opcodes (ASK2 ehash
+	 * records) grow the frame in front of its start when they push a
+	 * VLAN tag onto an untagged frame; with no internal margin that
+	 * wedges the RX port (RX-deaf until a cold power-cycle). The vendor
+	 * SDK reserves 96 B here and starts parsing after it (RIM
+	 * 0x60000000, RPSO 0x60, read live on .106). Same values here: with
+	 * them, untagged->VLAN push offloads at line rate and every other
+	 * path (kernel RX, routed, VLAN pop/translate) is unchanged
+	 * [SILICON 2026-10-05, .185].
+	 */
+	tmp = ((max_t(u32, cfg->int_buf_start_margin,
+		      FMAN_PORT_RX_HM_MARGIN) / PORT_IC_OFFSET_UNITS) &
 		BMI_INT_BUF_MARG_MASK) << BMI_INT_BUF_MARG_SHIFT;
 	iowrite32be(tmp, &regs->fmbm_rim);
+	iowrite32be(FMAN_PORT_RX_HM_MARGIN, &regs->fmbm_rpso);
 
 	/* External buffer margins */
 	tmp = (cfg->buf_margins.start_margins & BMI_EXT_BUF_MARG_START_MASK) <<
